              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "beachgranny123"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My nephews mother-in law made this at there wedding 7yrs ago..loved it have made it a few times for partys and holidays...sooo good..addicting glad to see this..recived in my inbox...:)I never used the garlic or dry mustard but will give it a try."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "litg8r"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I grew up with Win Schulers bar cheese. My recipe calls for a pound of Velveeta melted in the microwave. I add about 3-4 tablespoons prepared horseradish, about a teaspoon Worcestershire sauce, and a couple dashes of hot sauce. I don't have exact measurements because I prepare by taste, but this is essentially my version, which I think comes real close to the Win Schulers version. The mixture needs to be refrigerated and the flavors really blend and come out with time. Serve with rye toast. To die for!",
            "datePublished": "2025-05-27T22:55:42.066Z"
          },
          {
