            },
            "reviewBody": "I agree with the author. I live in the South now, but this brought back happy memories! Thank you!",
            "datePublished": "2019-04-22T02:06:04.783Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Meredith DeLorenzo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Tasty cheese spread I made with a block of Kraft extra sharp cheddar cheese. I melted the cheese on the stove and added a splash of milk. Since the cheese block was 8 ounces, I made half the recipe, so I estimated the garlic powder. It's a good imitation of Win Schuler cheese.",
            "datePublished": "2019-04-18T15:29:32.657Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Nathan Gehman"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love Win Schulers Bar Cheese as I was growing up in Southeastern Michigan. Gordon Food Service used to have their version called 'Tavern Cheese Spread' in their retail stores here in Florida. I'd buy it a case at a time but when I went back to resupply, they discontinued it..\n\nOH NOOOOO!!! I gotta have my fix, especially with upcoming football parties.\n\nNow that I've found the recipe, I'll just make my own!!",
            "datePublished": "2018-08-12T17:33:56.347Z"
          }
